    {
      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the area of the square, we need to determine the length of its side. We are given two expressions for the length of the side: \\(4x - 15\\) meters and \\(20 - 3x\\) meters. Since both expressions represent the length of the same side, we can set them equal to each other and solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[4x - 15 = 20 - 3x\\]\n\nFirst, we add \\(3x\\) to both sides of the equation to get all the \\(x\\) terms on one side:\n\n\\[4x + 3x - 15 = 20\\]\n\\[7x - 15 = 20\\]\n\nNext, we add 15 to both sides to isolate the term with \\(x\\):\n\n\\[7x = 20 + 15\\]\n\\[7x = 35\\]\n\nNow, we divide both sides by 7 to solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[x = \\frac{35}{7}\\]\n\\[x = 5\\]\n\nWith \\(x\\) determined, we substitute \\(x = 5\\) back into either expression for the side length to find the actual length of the side. We can use either expression, but let's use \\(4x - 15\\):\n\n\\[4(5) - 15 = 20 - 15 = 5\\]\n\nSo, the length of the side of the square is 5 meters. The area \\(A\\) of a square is given by the square of the length of its side:\n\n\\[A = 5^2 = 25\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{25}\\) square meters.",
